                "3. The Newspapers (Incitement to Offences) Act (1908): Empowered magistrates to confiscate printing presses of newspapers publishing articles inciting rebellion or violence.",
                "4. The Indian Criminal Law Amendment Act (1908): Banned nationalist volunteer corps and samitis; provided for summary trials by special three-judge tribunals without a jury.",
                "5. The Indian Press Act of 1910: Re-imposed heavy security deposits and strict censorship on all Indian newspapers.",
                "Banishments & Deportations: Under Regulation III of 1818, Lala Lajpat Rai and Sardar Ajit Singh were deported without trial to Mandalay in May 1907; Ashwini Kumar Dutt, Krishna Kumar Mitra, and seven other Bengal leaders were deported in December 1908.",
