                "First Indian in Viceroy's Executive Council: Satyendra Prasanna Sinha (S.P. Sinha, later Lord Sinha) was appointed as the first Indian Law Member in the Viceroy's Executive Council (1909).",
                "Introduction of Separate Electorates: The most sinister, fateful provision; introduced communal representation for Muslims.",
                "Mechanics of Separate Electorate: Muslim seats could be contested only by Muslims, and voted upon exclusively by Muslim voters; income and property qualifications for Muslim voters were kept deliberately lower than for Hindu voters.",
                "Lord Minto is known as the 'Father of Communal Electorate in India'.",
                "Morley's Confession: Lord Morley wrote to Minto: 'We are sowing dragon's teeth, and the harvest will be bitter.'",
                "Nationalist Condemnation: The Indian National Congress at its 1909 Lahore session (presided over by Madan Mohan Malaviya) condemned the communal electorates as a calculated imperialist conspiracy to institutionalize religious division and destroy Indian nationhood.",
