                "Montagu's Historic Declaration (20 August 1917): Edwin Montagu (Secretary of State) announced in the British House of Commons that British policy was the 'increasing association of Indians in every branch of administration, and the gradual development of self-governing institutions, with a view to the progressive realization of responsible government in India as an integral part of the British Empire' (known as the 'August Declaration').",
